          "concern": "A general URL/non-URL scope exclusion is too broad for a Microsoft-specific offline_access response difference.",
          "response": "darktrojan requests a focused Microsoft exception in1217884, while1217894/1217896 ask for explanatory comments, placement and sentence punctuation. All four submitted request markers are Done. darktrojan later explicitly accepts, but the system also records landing in Needs Review; no all-reviewer acceptance is inferred.",
          "applied": "The selected diff restores offline_access in MICROSOFT_SCOPES. At the exact common Microsoft token endpoint it adds a missing offline_access to returnedScopes before comparison and saving. It retains other scope discrepancies as warnings. The frozen code broadens the endpoint check to the Microsoft tenant prefix, as later accepted context.",
